WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们带来终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:26.670
Hey there.
嘿。

9
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:27.590
How are ya?
你好吗？

10
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:28.250
I'm good.
我很好。

11
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:28.850
How are you?
你呢？

12
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:29.910
I'm sluggish.
我感觉懒洋洋的。

13
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:30.650
You are?
是吗？

14
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.210
I think it's the heat.
我觉得是因为天气太热了。

15
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.130
Well, it's very hot.
是啊，确实很热。

16
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.670
It's very hot.
非常热。

17
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.650
I'm wearing one of those dresses that doesn't touch you anywhere.
我穿了一条那种完全不贴身的裙子。

18
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.430
Yeah, it's so hot.
是啊，太热了。

19
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.130
It's too hot.
热得过分了。

20
00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.790
I'm wearing flip-flops.
我穿着人字拖。

21
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.570
I never do that when we record.
录音的时候我从不穿人字拖。

22
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.570
Oh, I wear them all the time.
哦，我经常穿。

23
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:47.490
When we record?
录音的时候？

24
00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.150
Yeah, look at my feet right now.
对啊，你看我的脚。

25
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.150
Oh, yeah.
哦，看到了。

26
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:51.690
There you go.
就是这样。

27
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.180
Well, now that you know what we're wearing, Jenna, what are you wearing?
好了，既然你知道我们穿什么了，珍娜，你穿的是什么？

28
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.180
I am wearing these, like, black, what would you call them?
我穿的是这种黑色的，该怎么形容呢？

29
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.620
They're like the big leg pants.
就像那种大裤腿的裤子。

30
00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.680
Well, these are, like, my find of the year.
这可是我今年的心头好。

31
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.240
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

32
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.740
A mom friend of mine, she's French.
我有个妈妈朋友，她是法国人。

33
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:10.320
No.
不会吧。

34
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.660
She has the cutest pants all the time.
她总是穿着最可爱的裤子。

35
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:14.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

36
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.940
Of course, she's French.
当然了，她是法国人嘛。

37
00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.200
She's got the style.
她很有品位。

38
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:17.380
She's chic.
她很时髦。

39
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:17.760
She's chic.
她很时髦。

40
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.200
Yes.
没错。

41
00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.740
She told me about them, and they're very cool.
她告诉了我这个牌子，真的很棒。

42
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.180
They're very billowy.
裤子非常飘逸。

43
00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.720
And then I have on a cool billowy black top to go with it.
我还搭了一件很酷的飘逸黑色上衣。

44
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.580
I'm billowy.
我整个人都很飘逸。

45
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.400
You're billowy.
你确实很飘逸。

46
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.360
I'm in a big, flowy dress from Tarragut.
我穿的是一件来自Tarragut的大号飘逸裙子。

47
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:31.200
Okay.
好的。

48
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:31.780
Okay.
好的。

49
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:32.620
Now.
现在。

50
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.060
Target.
是Target。

51
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:33.800
Target.
目标。

52
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.440
It's also French.
它也是法语。

53
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.580
So, now that we've got that out of the way, what are we talking about today?
好了，既然这些都处理完了，我们今天聊什么呢？

54
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.300
I loved this episode.
我超爱这一集。

55
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.560
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

56
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:43.820
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

57
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.660
I was so excited for these storylines.
我对这些剧情线感到非常兴奋。

58
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:52.440
Is it any surprise that we love this episode now that our characters finally have stories again?
我们的角色终于又有了故事，我们喜欢这一集难道还奇怪吗？

59
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.040
Could that be part of it?
这会是原因之一吗？

60
00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:54.480
That could.
有可能。

61
00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.920
Maybe it's because our characters make it better.
也许是因为我们的角色让它变得更精彩了。

62
00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.020
Well, we have it on very good authority from the writer's room.
嗯，我们从编剧室那里得到了非常可靠的消息。

63
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.180
That's right.
没错。

64
00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.620
Yes, Steve Healy said.
是的，史蒂夫·希利说了。

65
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.180
More Pam and Angela.
多点帕姆和安吉拉的戏份。

66
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.440
Pam and Angela.
帕姆和安吉拉。

67
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.540
It's official, and this episode proves it.
这是官方认证的，这一集就证明了这一点。

68
00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:10.720
We're talking about jury duty.
我们要聊的是陪审团义务。

69
00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.180
We finally got there.
我们终于聊到这儿了。

70
00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.660
It's season eight, episode 13, written by Aaron Schur, who we love.
这是第八季第13集，由我们喜爱的亚伦·舒尔编剧。

71
00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:17.100
Love.
超爱。

72
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.740
And directed by Eric Appel.
由埃里克·阿佩尔执导。

73
00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.160
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

74
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.140
Jim is back from jury duty.
吉姆结束陪审团义务回来了。

75
00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.240
Or is he?
真的是这样吗？

76
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:23.800
Hmm.
嗯。

77
00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.920
Turns out he was actually home helping Pam with the kids.
事实证明，他其实一直待在家里帮帕姆照顾孩子。

78
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.480
Dwight figures this out and is determined to get Jim fired as a result.
德怀特发现了这一点，并决心因此让吉姆被解雇。

79
00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:40.620
Also, Angela gives birth to a big, healthy preemie, which causes some speculation about timelines and paternity.
此外，安吉拉生下了一个又大又健康的早产儿，这引起了一些关于时间线和亲子关系的猜测。

80
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:41.440
Oh, man.
天呐。

81
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.820
And Pam brings CeCe and Philip into the office to visit.
帕姆带着西西和菲利普到办公室探班。

82
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:49.240
Fast fact number one, new director alert, Eric Appel.
速递事实第一条，新导演预警，埃里克·阿佩尔。

83
00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.560
Eric has directed a ton of television.
埃里克执导过大量的电视节目。

84
00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:57.340
His background is in animation and sketch comedy, and he did improv at the Upright Citizens Brigade.
他的背景是动画和素描喜剧，他还在“直立公民旅”做过即兴表演。

85
00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.660
Eric was fantastic.
埃里克太棒了。

86
00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:00.220
Fantastic.
太棒了。

87
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.560
I'm going to get there.
我一会儿会讲到。

88
00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.060
There's a scene between Dwight and Angela where he just let us go.
德怀特和安吉拉之间有一场戏，他完全让我们自由发挥。

89
00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.540
I think I know which one.
我想我知道是哪一场。

90
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.180
I think you do.
我想你肯定知道。

91
00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:08.880
Because I loved it.
因为我太喜欢那场戏了。

92
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.640
But Eric has been nominated for and won several awards for his work.
埃里克凭借他的作品获得过多次奖项提名并获奖。

93
00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:20.160
According to his IMDb page under the trivia section, Eric can trifold his tongue.
根据他IMDb页面上的琐事部分，埃里克可以把舌头折成三折。

94
00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:21.360
What?
什么？

95
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.440
This is also sometimes referred to as a cloverleaf tongue.
这有时也被称为三叶草舌。

96
00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.280
What is a trifold tongue?
什么是三折舌？

97
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.680
I had to Google it.
我不得不去谷歌了一下。

98
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.060
I don't understand.
我不明白。

99
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.820
Is that where you make it look like a flower kind of thing?
就是那种让舌头看起来像朵花一样的东西吗？

100
00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.840
Well, you tell me.
嗯，你告诉我。

101
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.240
I think it looks like a W, like you're making a W with your tongue.
我觉得它看起来像个W，就像你用舌头做出了一个W的形状。

102
00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.640
While Googling what it was, I found out that Daniel Radcliffe can also do this.
在谷歌搜索它是什么的时候，我发现丹尼尔·雷德克里夫也能做到这一点。

103
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.940
And here, Daniel Radcliffe did it once on a red carpet.
你看，丹尼尔·雷德克里夫在红毯上就做过一次。

104
00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:50.040
There's Daniel Radcliffe's trifold tongue.
这就是丹尼尔·雷德克里夫的三折舌头。

105
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:51.300
Wow.
哇。

106
00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:52.060
Yeah.
是啊。

107
00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.600
That's impressive.
真令人印象深刻。

108
00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.480
I know.
我知道。

109
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.440
Okay.
好吧。

110
00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.000
Well.
嗯。

111
00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:05.340
According to an article on Colgate.com, 14.7% of the population can trifold their tongue.
根据Colgate.com上的一篇文章，14.7%的人口可以把舌头折成三折。

112
00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.100
Can anyone here?
这里有人能做到吗？

113
00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:07.580
Sam?
萨姆？

114
00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.120
Cassie?
凯西？

115
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.580
Anyone trifold your tongue?
有人能把舌头折成三折吗？

116
00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:10.020
I cannot.
我做不到。

117
00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.140
Jenna clearly can't.
珍娜显然做不到。

118
00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.120
She had to Google it.
她还得去谷歌搜索一下。

119
00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:12.440
Hold on.
等等。

120
00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.220
Cassie's looking it up to see if she can.
凯西正在查她自己能不能做到。

121
00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.760
It looks like a W.
看起来像个W。

122
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:16.320
It really looks like a W.
真的看起来像个W。

123
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.320
Can you make a W out of your tongue?
你能用舌头做出W的形状吗？

124
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.780
I can do the canoe thing with my tongue.
我能用舌头做出独木舟的样子。

125
00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.540
I can do the canoe fold.
我能做独木舟折叠。

126
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.160
And I can also fold my tongue in half like this.
而且我还能像这样把舌头对折。

127
00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:28.160
Oh, my God.
天哪。

128
00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.940
That makes the grossest sound.
那发出的声音太恶心了。

129
00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.420
Oh, no.
噢，不。

130
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.960
Well, it keeps popping up.
好吧，它一直在弹出来。

131
00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.300
It was really gross.
真的太恶心了。

132
00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:36.820
So sorry, everyone.
非常抱歉，各位。

133
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.240
I had no idea we were going here this morning.
我没想到今天早上会聊到这个话题。

134
00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.080
Well, you never know.
嗯，谁知道呢。

135
00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:44.520
Listen.
听着。

136
00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:44.780
You know what?
你知道吗？

137
00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.560
It's where my research took us.
这就是我的研究把我们带到的地方。

138
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.280
I love it.
我喜欢。

139
00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.060
Would you like Fast Fact No.
你想要第二个速览事实吗？

140
00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:49.400
2?
2？

141
00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.320
I can't wait.
我迫不及待了。

142
00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.240
Fast Fact No.
速览事实第

143
00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.080
2 is a fan question from Tracy W.
2条是来自挪威的特蕾西·W的粉丝提问。

144
00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:53.840
in Norway.
在挪威。

145
00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.820
Jenna and Angela, I'm curious if you have ever had any interesting real-life personal experiences
珍娜和安吉拉，我很好奇你们是否有过任何有趣的现实生活经历

146
00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.660
being summoned for jury duty.
关于被传唤去担任陪审员的。

147
00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.080
Tracy, I almost always get selected to be on a jury.
特蕾西，我几乎每次都会被选中担任陪审员。

148
00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.960
I mean, every time I go in there, they're like, little blonde lady, get up here.
我是说，每次我进去，他们就像是，那个金发小个子女士，上来吧。

149
00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.820
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

150
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.900
But yes, I have many stories of jury duty.
但是是的，我有很多关于陪审团职责的故事。

151
00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.300
I think I've already shared one.
我想我已经分享过一个了。

152
00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.920
Yeah, back when Toby had jury duty.
没错，就在托比去当陪审员的时候。

153
00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:22.300
Right.
对。

154
00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.980
That was when I was a juror on a bait car case.
那是我在诱饵车案件中担任陪审员的时候。

155
00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.340
But guess what I found in my digital clutter?
但你猜我在我的数字杂物里发现了什么？

156
00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.540
And I didn't even know you had this question.
而且我甚至都不知道你问过这个问题。

157
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:31.020
What?
什么？

158
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:38.180
I wrote you an email from one of the many times I was waiting to be, you know, picked for
我给你写过一封邮件，那是我等待被选中去当陪审员的

159
00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:38.620
a jury.
那段时间里写的。

160
00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:39.740
And I found it.
我把它找出来了。

161
00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:39.980
Ready?
准备好了吗？

162
00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:40.500
Okay.
好。

163
00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.880
I love this.
我喜欢这个。

164
00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.140
This is from October 2018.
这是2018年10月的。

165
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.340
All right.
好吧。

166
00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:45.620
Okay.
好的。

167
00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:46.700
I wrote this.
这是我写的。

168
00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.040
And I sent you a picture, too.
我还给你发了一张照片。

169
00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.680
I took a selfie there.
我在那儿自拍了一张。

170
00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.840
In the waiting room, guys, I wasn't in the courthouse, okay?
在候审室里，伙计们，我当时不在法庭里，好吗？

171
00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:54.300
Okay.
好的。

172
00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:54.780
That's right.
没错。

173
00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.200
You're not allowed to do that in the courthouse.
在法庭里是不允许那样做的。

174
00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.920
But in that holding room, you can.
但在那个等候室里，是可以的。

175
00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:58.960
Okay.
好吧。

176
00:05:59.060 --> 00:05:59.980
Here's what I emailed you.
这是我发给你的邮件内容。

177
00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:01.080
Hey, lady.
嘿，女士。

178
00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:02.280
Day two.
第二天。

179
00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.760
I'm waiting to see if I get picked for a jury.
我正在等候看是否会被选中去当陪审员。

180
00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.060
I'm sitting in a big room with a bunch of people.
我正坐在一间大屋子里，和一群人在一起。

181
00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.160
And we all have those chairs from high school that have a mini desk attached to them.
我们坐的都是那种高中里带小课桌的椅子。

182
00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.200
I feel like I'm in a study hall at a school for random adults.
我觉得自己就像是在一所面向随机成年人的自习室里。

183
00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.080
I brought townhouse crackers and some cheese.
我带了汤豪斯饼干和一些奶酪。

184
00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:23.820
And the guy next to me looks up every time I bite into a cracker.
我旁边的那个人每次我咬一口饼干，他都会抬头看我。

185
00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.980
I also brought my laptop and have Wi-Fi.
我还带了笔记本电脑，而且有Wi-Fi。

186
00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.600
So email away or leave me a message.
所以尽管发邮件或给我留言吧。

187
00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.680
I have headphones.
我有耳机。

188
00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.460
You wrote back.
你回信了。

189
00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.800
You look amazing.
你看上去棒极了。

190
00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.240
Why do you have such pretty hair for jury duty?
为什么你去当陪审员头发还弄得这么漂亮？

191
00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:43.650
God, Angela, you brought cheese to jury duty.
天哪，安吉拉，你竟然带了奶酪去当陪审员。

192
00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:44.950
And townhouse crackers.
还有汤豪斯饼干。

193
00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.510
It's so you.
这太像你了。

194
00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:51.890
And I took a selfie and you see me holding like a Ziploc of crackers.
我还自拍了一张，照片里你能看到我拿着一袋密封的饼干。

195
00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:55.210
Oh, that's incredible.
噢，太不可思议了。

196
00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.270
That is incredible.
那真是太不可思议了。

197
00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:58.510
All right.
好吧。

198
00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.050
I have a crazy story.
我有一个疯狂的故事。

199
00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:00.530
Okay.
好的。

200
00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.150
I was on jury duty the week we were prepping this episode to record.
就在我们准备录制这一集的那周，我正好在当陪审员。

201
00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:07.630
That is crazy.
太疯狂了。

202
00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:08.310
Jury duty.
陪审团义务。

203
00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.510
That is crazy.
太疯狂了。

204
00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:10.950
But it was a mistake.
但那是个失误。

205
00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.050
What do you mean?
你什么意思？

206
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.270
So.
所以。

207
00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:13.810
How?
怎么会？

208
00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:14.490
What?
什么？

209
00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:14.670
Okay.
好吧。

210
00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.890
So I was supposed to do jury duty.
我本来应该去履行陪审团义务的。

211
00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:17.470
Yeah.
嗯。

212
00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:18.910
And I broke my shoulder.
结果我摔断了肩膀。

213
00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:19.910
And I couldn't drive.
我没法开车。

214
00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.770
I couldn't go.
去不了。

215
00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:21.130
Yeah.
是啊。

216
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.650
So I postponed it.
所以我申请了延期。

217
00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:23.190
Sure.
当然。

218
00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:25.670
But I forgot to when I postponed it.
但我忘了自己是什么时候申请延期的。

219
00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.870
And suddenly it popped up on my calendar.
突然它就在我的日历上弹出来了。

220
00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.510
I got a reminder on the Sunday night before.
我在周日晚上收到了提醒。

221
00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.430
My husband was out of town the whole week.
我丈夫那一整周都不在城里。

222
00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:35.190
Lee was gone.
李出差了。

223
00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:36.610
He had to go to Chicago.
他得去芝加哥。

224
00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.070
And I was the only parent.
家里只有我一个家长。

225
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.190
And I thought, oh my gosh, I can't.
我心想，天哪，我没法去。

226
00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.130
I'm the only one home.
家里只有我一个人。

227
00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.650
I can't do it.
我没法去。

228
00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.010
What if I get picked for a jury?
万一我被选进陪审团了怎么办？

229
00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.650
So I can't do jury duty.
所以我没法履行陪审义务。

230
00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:48.070
No.
不行。

231
00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.030
So I go on the computer.
于是我上网操作。

232
00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.330
They have a portal.
他们有个门户网站。

233
00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:52.830
You log in with your juror ID number.
用你的陪审员编号登录就行。

234
00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:53.310
Yes.
没错。

235
00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.630
And so I go to the portal and it says you can't postpone anymore.
我登录了网站，上面显示不能再延期了。

236
00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.770
You had to do that by the Friday before.
必须在之前的周五前完成申请。

237
00:07:59.030 --> 00:07:59.210
Yeah.
是啊。

238
00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:03.630
But it also said you don't have to report tomorrow, Monday.
但它也说周一不用去报到。

239
00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.630
Check in again Monday evening to see if you have to report Tuesday.
周一晚上再查一次，看周二是否需要报到。

240
00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.450
So you just rolled the dice.
所以你就是在碰运气。

241
00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.670
You had to.
只能这样。

242
00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:11.210
I did.
我确实是。

243
00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.590
I rolled the dice.
我在碰运气。

244
00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:17.030
Every night at 7 p.m., I would log into my jury portal.
每天晚上七点，我都会登录陪审团门户网站。

245
00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:19.310
And every night it said you don't have to report.
每天晚上它都显示不需要报到。

246
00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:23.150
And then on Thursday night, it said you've completed your jury duty.
然后周四晚上，它显示我已经完成了陪审义务。

247
00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:24.150
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

248
00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:24.470
Amazing.
太神奇了。

249
00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.070
I completed it by mistake.
我阴差阳错地完成了。

250
00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.850
How lucky was I?
我得有多幸运啊？

251
00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:29.690
Very lucky.
非常幸运。

252
00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:32.730
I mean, considering everything, you were like single parenting.
我是说，考虑到种种情况，你当时就像是在独自抚养孩子。

253
00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:33.230
Yes.
是的。

254
00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:39.470
I will say, anyone that knows our mom detective hearts knows that we would actually be thrilled
我想说，任何了解我们那颗“侦探妈妈”心的人都知道，我们其实会很兴奋

255
00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:42.810
to get picked under different circumstances.
能在不同情况下被选中。

256
00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:43.530
Yeah.
是啊。

257
00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:46.330
I've reported many times and I've never been selected.
我报到过很多次，但从来没被选中过。

258
00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.410
Oh, I always get selected and I get very excited.
噢，我总是被选中，而且我非常兴奋。

259
00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.370
That tracks.
这很符合你的性格。

260
00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:51.810
Yeah.
是啊。

261
00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.690
And I bring a notepad and a pen.
而且我会带上记事本和笔。

262
00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.470
And some people know I'm serious.
有些人知道我是认真的。

263
00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.930
Maybe that's why you're getting picked.
也许这就是你总被选中的原因。

264
00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:00.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

265
00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.650
Well, those are our jury duty stories.
好吧，这就是我们的陪审团故事。

266
00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:05.870
Moving us now to Fast Fact 3.
现在进入第三个速览事实。

267
00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.770
I titled it, Pam is Back.
我给它起名为：帕姆回归。

268
00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:08.490
Yes.
没错。

269
00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.230
Pam is back.
帕姆回归了。

270
00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:09.910
Pam is back.
帕姆回归了。

271
00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:14.170
Everyone, I did this episode five weeks after having a C-section.
各位，我是在剖腹产五周后拍摄的这一集。

272
00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.770
I did that because actors do not get paid maternity leave.
我之所以这么做，是因为演员没有带薪产假。

273
00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:18.590
That is true.
确实如此。

274
00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.870
We go on unpaid disability, which means your employer can't fire you,
我们休的是无薪伤残假，这意味着雇主不能解雇你，

275
00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.430
but they do not have to pay you.
但他们不必支付你工资。

276
00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:24.870
Yep.
没错。

277
00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.490
So every time I missed an episode, I missed a paycheck.
所以每次我缺席一集拍摄，就意味着少了一份薪水。

278
00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:29.210
That's right.
没错。

279
00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.710
I wrote about it in our book.
我在我们的书里写过这件事。

280
00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.070
Yeah.
是啊。

281
00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.350
We got a lot of mail about this.
我们收到了很多关于此事的来信。

282
00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.870
People who had read our book and were surprised to learn about this.
读过我们书的人对了解到这一点感到惊讶。

283
00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:37.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

284
00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.550
We got a fan question from Kathleen M.
我们收到了一位来自北卡罗来纳州的凯瑟琳·M的粉丝提问，

285
00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.330
in North Carolina who said,
她问道：

286
00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:45.770
In your book, The Office BFFs, Jenna shared about how hard it was for her to return and
在你们的书《办公室闺蜜》中，珍娜分享了她在生完孩子后回到剧组

287
00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.870
film this episode after having her baby and how supportive everyone was.
拍摄这一集有多么困难，以及大家是如何支持她的。

288
00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:54.650
I'd love to hear more about what it was like to film an episode of TV right after having your
我很想多了解一下，刚生完孩子就去拍摄电视剧是什么感觉，

289
00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:58.030
baby and what was going through your head when filming these scenes.
以及你在拍摄这些场景时心里在想些什么。

290
00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.070
Well, Kathleen, it was very, very hard.
嗯，凯瑟琳，那真的非常、非常困难。

291
00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.050
I could not walk without pain.
我走路时感到疼痛难忍。

292
00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.350
I was uncomfortable.
我浑身不适。

293
00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.010
I was still bleeding.
我还在出血。

294
00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:11.850
As you bleed a lot after you have a baby, it doesn't matter if it's C-section or vaginal.
因为生完孩子后确实会流很多血，不管是剖腹产还是顺产都一样。

295
00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:12.290
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

296
00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:16.730
I was still working with a lactation consultant trying to get my son to nurse well.
我当时还在咨询哺乳顾问，努力让儿子顺利吃奶。

297
00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:20.450
I was very worried about messing up his feeding schedule.
我非常担心会打乱他的喂养时间表。

298
00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:26.150
At the same time, coming back to work meant that I got to see all of these people who just
与此同时，回到工作岗位意味着我能见到所有那些非常爱我的人，

299
00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:30.950
loved me so much, the cast and the crew, and I'd been very isolated at home.
包括演员和剧组工作人员，而我之前在家里一直很孤立。

300
00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:33.490
Parents know this when you have a new baby.
有新生儿的父母都懂这种感觉。

301
00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:38.450
We get letters from people who tell us we're keeping them company at home in those early
我们收到过很多来信，人们说我们在他们最初的那些日子里陪伴着他们，

302
00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.070
months.
那些月份里。

303
00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:44.090
I remember loving having friends that had a big time difference who were already awake.
我记得当时很庆幸有身处不同时区、已经醒着的朋友。

304
00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:48.910
You know, my friends on the East Coast because I would be up at like 4 a.m.
你知道，比如我在东海岸的朋友，因为我那时凌晨四点左右就会醒来。

305
00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:49.250
Yeah.
是啊。

306
00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:53.010
And I knew I could call and just kind of talk to them while I breastfed.
我知道我可以给他们打电话，在哺乳的时候和他们聊聊天。

307
00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:56.750
Well, the part of getting to see people, I loved that.
嗯，能见到人这一点，我真的很喜欢。

308
00:10:56.930 --> 00:11:02.290
That was good for my soul because I'd been very, like, in a cocoon, you know?
这对我的心灵很有治愈作用，因为我当时就像一直待在蚕茧里一样，你懂吗？

309
00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:02.490
Yeah.
是啊。

310
00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.970
And then when we started filming, my adrenaline really kicked in.
后来我们开始拍摄时，我的肾上腺素真的飙升了。

311
00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:07.190
It was almost dreamlike.
那感觉简直像做梦一样。

312
00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:11.950
I don't have any real memories that when I watched that scene, I feel like I dreamed
我没什么真实的记忆，看那场戏的时候，我觉得自己好像是梦到过

313
00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:12.250
it.
它一样。

314
00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.650
I was like, I guess I was there.
我当时心想，我猜我当时确实在那儿吧。

315
00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:19.530
So we also got another letter from Alexis Kaye in California who said,
我们还收到了一封来自加州 Alexis Kaye 的来信，她说：

316
00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:22.890
Jenna, after listening to your experience in your book about coming back to work,
Jenna，读了你书中关于产后重返职场的经历，

317
00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:25.570
just five weeks after having your baby, I'm floored.
在生完孩子仅仅五周后就回去工作，我简直惊呆了。

318
00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:29.750
I also had a C-section, and I can't imagine going back to work that quickly.
我也经历过剖腹产，我无法想象那么快就回去工作。

319
00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:33.570
I am so in awe and just wanted to say that you looked amazing.
我真的非常佩服你，只是想说你当时看起来状态太棒了。

320
00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:38.030
You looked peaceful, glowing, and at ease, although I'm sure you were so overwhelmed
你看上去平静、容光焕发且从容不迫，尽管我肯定你当时一定

321
00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.150
with many emotions.
百感交集，压力巨大。

322
00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:43.310
You mentioned in the book that Angela and the rest of the cast and crew were really supportive.
你在书中提到 Angela 和其他演职人员都非常支持你。

323
00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:47.230
What else helped you in those first weeks of going back to work?
在重返职场的最初几周，还有什么帮到了你吗？

324
00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:51.210
Well, my husband, Lee, was amazing.
嗯，我的丈夫 Lee，他真的很棒。

325
00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.570
We eventually had to hire a nanny, but we had not done that yet.
我们最终不得不请了一位保姆，但当时还没请。

326
00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:56.610
It was five weeks.
那才五周大。

327
00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:56.950
Yeah.
是啊。

328
00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.530
We were like still figuring out how to swaddle.
我们当时还在研究怎么给孩子裹襁褓呢。

329
00:11:59.670 --> 00:11:59.870
Yeah.
是啊。

330
00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.310
So for this episode, he came to work with me.
所以拍这一集的时候，他陪我一起去工作了。

331
00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:05.890
He had our son in my trailer with him so that I could nurse him.
他带着我们的儿子在我的房车里，这样我就能给他喂奶。

332
00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:08.670
Because like I said, I was still trying to get that down.
因为就像我说的，我当时还在努力适应哺乳这件事。

333
00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.150
So that was really helpful.
所以那真的很有帮助。

334
00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:15.250
And I would have to shout out our first AD, Kelly Cantley, because she was instrumental
我必须得感谢我们的第一副导演 Kelly Cantley，因为她对

335
00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.830
in making that happen.
促成这件事起到了关键作用。

336
00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.310
Here's what she told me.
她是这样跟我说的。

337
00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:23.910
She got me aside, and she said, Jenna, I am legally required to let you leave set to pump
她把我拉到一边说：Jenna，法律规定我必须让你离开片场去用吸奶器

338
00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:24.190
milk.
吸奶。

339
00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:28.450
I am not legally required to let you nurse your baby.
