她说，

725
00:26:34.450 --> 00:26:39.770
we know Gabe has weird fears, like his fear of cockroaches and getting squeamish around babies.
我们知道盖博有一些奇怪的恐惧症，比如他怕蟑螂，而且一看到婴儿就感到不适。

726
00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:45.290
But I guess he got over his fear of babies because here he says he loves going to maternity warts.
但我猜他克服了对婴儿的恐惧，因为他在这里说他喜欢去产房。

727
00:26:45.290 --> 00:26:48.890
Is this a continuity error or did he get over this fear?
这是一个连续性错误，还是他真的克服了这个恐惧？

728
00:26:49.290 --> 00:26:51.870
Well, Afrin, I don't think he got over his fear.
嗯，Afrin，我不认为他克服了恐惧。

729
00:26:52.050 --> 00:26:57.570
I think he's doing that thing where he's, like, walking into the spooky funhouse.
我觉得他就像那种走进恐怖游乐屋的人。

730
00:26:58.290 --> 00:27:03.030
He's going to be creeped out when he sees the babies, but there's something about him that's drawn to it.
他看到婴儿时会感到毛骨悚然，但又有什么东西吸引着他。

731
00:27:03.190 --> 00:27:04.070
That's what I got.
我是这么理解的。

732
00:27:04.870 --> 00:27:09.570
Well, I think he's drawn to the process of the babies coming into the world.
嗯，我觉得他被婴儿来到这个世界的过程所吸引。

733
00:27:10.210 --> 00:27:10.710
Hmm.
嗯。

734
00:27:10.710 --> 00:27:11.390
Labor.
分娩。

735
00:27:11.650 --> 00:27:13.150
I think he's drawn to labor.
我觉得他被分娩过程吸引了。

736
00:27:14.170 --> 00:27:14.570
Really?
真的吗？

737
00:27:14.890 --> 00:27:15.130
Yeah.
是的。

738
00:27:15.330 --> 00:27:16.190
That's my theory.
这是我的理论。

739
00:27:16.930 --> 00:27:18.930
It's odd any way you look at it.
不管怎么看都很奇怪。

740
00:27:18.930 --> 00:27:19.570
It sure is.
确实如此。

741
00:27:19.590 --> 00:27:20.550
Gabe is an odd bird.
盖博是个怪人。

742
00:27:20.990 --> 00:27:24.350
Well, a bunch of people start having excuses why they're not going to go, right?
嗯，很多人开始找借口不去，对吧？

743
00:27:24.570 --> 00:27:26.190
Jim says, oh, I've missed too much work.
吉姆说，哦，我耽误的工作太多了。

744
00:27:26.190 --> 00:27:28.390
And Phyllis has this thing where she kind of trails off.
菲利斯说话总是那种欲言又止的样子。

745
00:27:28.470 --> 00:27:31.150
