00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:34.920
So many confessions have happened in this stairwell.
在这个楼梯间里发生过太多次坦白了。

1008
00:37:35.040 --> 00:37:37.100
It's where everyone goes for their heart-to-hearts.
这是每个人谈心的地方。

1009
00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:37.640
I know.
我知道。

1010
00:37:38.060 --> 00:37:39.120
It's very cute.
这很可爱。

1011
00:37:39.700 --> 00:37:41.620
I had a few heart-to-hearts in the stairwell.
我也曾在楼梯间里谈过几次心。

1012
00:37:41.840 --> 00:37:43.920
I had a big heart-to-heart in that stairwell.
我在那个楼梯间里进行过一次重要的谈心。

1013
00:37:44.100 --> 00:37:44.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1014
00:37:44.560 --> 00:37:45.180
Like, for real.
我是说真的。

1015
00:37:45.220 --> 00:37:45.740
For real.
真的。

1016
00:37:45.740 --> 00:37:46.980
I'm saying for real.
我没开玩笑，是真的。

1017
00:37:47.140 --> 00:37:47.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1018
00:37:47.360 --> 00:37:52.940
It kind of was funny that in episodes that were written, the characters had heart-to-hearts
剧本里写角色们在那里谈心，而现实生活中我们竟然也真的在那里谈过心，这挺有趣的。

1019
00:37:52.940 --> 00:37:55.320
there, but actually, in real life, we did too.
确实如此。

1020
00:37:55.540 --> 00:37:55.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1021
00:37:56.380 --> 00:37:58.340
Jim is going to tell Andy, look, I'm sorry.
吉姆打算告诉安迪，听着，我很抱歉。

1022
00:37:58.580 --> 00:38:02.500
I stayed home to help Pam with the kids, and I'm sorry I lied to you.
我待在家里是为了帮帕姆照顾孩子，我很抱歉对你撒了谎。

1023
00:38:02.860 --> 00:38:04.400
I think we should just come clean.
我觉得我们应该坦白。

1024
00:38:04.800 --> 00:38:05.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1025
00:38:05.240 --> 00:38:06.920
Jim says, I should tell everybody.
吉姆说，我应该告诉大家。

1026
00:38:06.920 --> 00:38:10.060
And Andy's like, no, no, no, no, no, no.
安迪却说，不，不，不，不，不，不。

1027
00:38:10.160 --> 00:38:11.800
This will be just between us.
这件事就我们俩知道就行了。

1028
00:38:12.520 --> 00:38:14.960
Yeah, because he doesn't want to, like, have to fire him.
是啊，因为他不想不得不解雇他。

1029
00:38:15.140 --> 00:38:15.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1030
00:38:15.640 --> 00:38:17.020
He's like, I got your back.
他说，我会罩着你的。

1031
00:38:17.180 --> 00:38:19.460
He's like, have you ever heard of a Connecticut cover-up?
他说，你听说过“康涅狄格掩盖法”吗？

1032
00:38:19.680 --> 00:38:20.460
Jim says, no.
吉姆说，没有。

1033
00:38:20.580 --> 00:38:22.620
Andy says, do you want to know why you never heard of it?
安迪说，你想知道为什么你从没听说过吗？

1034
00:38:22.700 --> 00:38:23.380
Jim says, no.
吉姆说，不想。

1035
00:38:23.580 --> 00:38:24.220
Covered it up.
因为被掩盖了。

1036
00:38:24.960 --> 00:38:26.400
That was a very funny couplet.
那是个非常有趣的双关语。

1037
00:38:26.580 --> 00:38:28.460
I looked up Connecticut cover-up.
我查了查“康涅狄格掩盖法”。

1038
00:38:28.580 --> 00:38:29.180
I did, too.
我也查了。

1039
00:38:29.340 --> 00:38:31.880
It's in the Urban Dictionary, attributed to the office.
它在城市词典里有收录，归功于《办公室》这部剧。

1040
00:38:32.060 --> 00:38:32.300
Right.
没错。

1041
00:38:32.520 --> 00:38:32.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1042
00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:38.040
I actually texted Warren about it, because he's from Connecticut, and I was like, Warren,
我其实还为此给沃伦发了短信，因为他是康涅狄格州人，我问他，沃伦，

1043
00:38:38.140 --> 00:38:39.400
was this you in the writer's room?
这是你在编剧室里想出来的吗？

1044
00:38:39.440 --> 00:38:43.560
He said, I can't take credit for it, but it feels like something I might have pitched.
他说，我不能居功，但这听起来确实像是我会提出的点子。

1045
00:38:44.200 --> 00:38:46.360
Well, Dwight has done something.
好吧，德怀特搞了点动作。

1046
00:38:47.180 --> 00:38:50.860
He has hired Ernesto's food truck to come to the office.
他雇了埃内斯托的餐车来办公室。

1047
00:38:51.080 --> 00:38:51.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1048
00:38:51.700 --> 00:38:52.900
Empanadas for everybody.
大家都有馅饼吃。

1049
00:38:53.500 --> 00:38:55.740
I asked Steve Burgess about that food truck.
我问过史蒂夫·伯吉斯关于那辆餐车的事。

1050
00:38:56.120 --> 00:38:59.320
He said that was a rental from Studio Picture Vehicles.
他说那是从制片厂车辆租赁公司租来的。

1051
00:38:59.340 --> 00:39:00.800
It really didn't make any food.
它真的没做出任何食物。

1052
00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:01.880
I didn't get any empanadas.
我没吃到任何馅饼。

1053
00:39:02.120 --> 00:39:02.260
No.
没有。

1054
00:39:02.560 --> 00:39:03.400
I wondered.
我当时就在想。

1055
00:39:03.780 --> 00:39:06.360
Well, immediately, Ernesto sees Toby.
嗯，埃内斯托一眼就看到了托比。

1056
00:39:06.620 --> 00:39:07.400
He's like, Toby!
他喊道：托比！

1057
00:39:07.940 --> 00:39:08.280
Yes.
没错。

1058
00:39:08.620 --> 00:39:11.500
And then Jim walks out, and Dwight's like, Jim, who's that?
然后吉姆走了出来，德怀特就问：吉姆，那是谁？

1059
00:39:12.060 --> 00:39:14.240
And Ernesto had no idea who he was.
而埃内斯托根本不知道他是谁。

1060
00:39:14.360 --> 00:39:15.580
And Jim had no idea.
吉姆也不知道。

1061
00:39:15.880 --> 00:39:16.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1062
00:39:16.560 --> 00:39:18.560
Clearly, until Toby's like, that's Ernesto.
显然，直到托比说：那是埃内斯托。

1063
00:39:18.560 --> 00:39:20.220
And Dwight's like, damn it!
德怀特就说：该死！

1064
00:39:20.400 --> 00:39:22.580
But he has a line that cracked me up.
但他有一句台词让我笑喷了。

1065
00:39:22.640 --> 00:39:27.040
He's like, okay, he remembers Toby, the most forgettable man in the known world.
他说，好吧，他记得托比，这个世界上最容易被遗忘的男人。

1066
00:39:27.860 --> 00:39:28.460
I know.
我知道。

1067
00:39:28.460 --> 00:39:32.800
So, guest star alert, Ernesto was played by Eduardo Antonio Garcia.
所以，客串明星预警，埃内斯托是由爱德华多·安东尼奥·加西亚饰演的。

1068
00:39:32.940 --> 00:39:37.120
You might recognize him from No Country for Old Men, for which he won a SAG award.
你可能在《老无所依》中见过他，他凭借该片获得了演员工会奖。

1069
00:39:37.320 --> 00:39:38.600
Or Law & Order LA.
或者《法律与秩序：洛杉矶》。

1070
00:39:38.760 --> 00:39:43.220
He is also one of the most prolific voice actors in the business.
他也是业内最多产的配音演员之一。

1071
00:39:43.220 --> 00:39:47.620
He has voiced over 1,500 commercials since 1998.
自1998年以来，他为超过1500条广告配过音。

1072
00:39:48.100 --> 00:39:48.920
That's amazing.
太厉害了。

1073
00:39:49.140 --> 00:39:49.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1074
00:39:49.900 --> 00:39:52.620
This scene has another one of my favorite lines in the episode.
这一幕里还有我这集里最喜欢的另一句台词。

1075
00:39:52.800 --> 00:39:53.040
Okay.
好的。

1076
00:39:53.640 --> 00:39:57.960
Creed says, usually, I'm a burrito guy, but if you won't tell, I won't.
克里德说：通常我只吃墨西哥卷饼，但如果你不说，我也不会说。

1077
00:39:58.120 --> 00:39:58.580
Wink, wink.
眨眼，眨眼。

1078
00:39:58.940 --> 00:39:59.840
Like, what?
就像是，什么鬼？

1079
00:40:00.440 --> 00:40:06.060
I just picture our writer's room just coming up with these non-sequitur, like, one-liners
我脑海中浮现出我们的编剧室，他们不断地为克里德想出这些不合逻辑的俏皮话。

1080
00:40:06.060 --> 00:40:07.280
for Creed constantly.
不断地。

1081
00:40:07.560 --> 00:40:09.280
See, this is why I'm not a writer.
你看，这就是为什么我当不了编剧。

1082
00:40:09.660 --> 00:40:12.620
Because I would just write the plot.
因为我只会写剧情。

1083
00:40:12.620 --> 00:40:18.780
There would be no of these little, like, awesome pops of flavor from different characters.
就不会有这些来自不同角色的、很棒的调味剂了。

1084
00:40:19.100 --> 00:40:21.040
All my characters would sound the same.
我笔下的所有角色听起来都会是一样的。

1085
00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:24.800
It would just be information, information, information.
那只会是信息，信息，还是信息。

1086
00:40:24.800 --> 00:40:26.160
Because that's what I do beSt.
因为那是我最擅长的。

1087
00:40:26.160 --> 00:40:28.520
I lay track, and I get you there.
我负责铺设轨道，把你带到目的地。

1088
00:40:28.700 --> 00:40:28.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1089
00:40:28.960 --> 00:40:31.080
But I don't know how to do all that other stuff.
但我不知道该怎么做其他那些东西。

1090
00:40:31.080 --> 00:40:32.000
It's so cool.
太酷了。

1091
00:40:32.180 --> 00:40:34.600
This is why we were such a good team writing our book.
这就是为什么我们在写书时是那么好的搭档。

1092
00:40:34.820 --> 00:40:37.700
Because I would write something, and you'd be like, Ange, this is really funny.
因为我写了一些东西，你会说：安吉，这真的很有趣。

1093
00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:38.760
This is a great memory.
这是一个很棒的回忆。

1094
00:40:39.240 --> 00:40:40.460
Where does it go?
它应该放在哪里？

1095
00:40:40.620 --> 00:40:41.980
I'm like, I don't know.
我说：我不知道。

1096
00:40:43.220 --> 00:40:45.360
And then you'd be like, okay, here's some structure.
然后你会说：好吧，这里需要一些结构。

1097
00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:48.320
And then you would write something, and I'd be like, Jenna, this is great.
然后你写了一些东西，我会说：珍娜，这太棒了。

1098
00:40:48.540 --> 00:40:51.080
I'm going to give it a little bit of zhush.
我要给它加点料润色一下。

1099
00:40:51.300 --> 00:40:51.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1100
00:40:51.600 --> 00:40:53.700
You're like, we need some jokes in here.
你会说：我们需要在这里加点笑话。

1101
00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:57.260
I am in awe of writers.
我真的很佩服作家。

1102
00:40:57.260 --> 00:41:00.760
It's no wonder that's who I would always fall in love with.
难怪我总是会爱上他们。

1103
00:41:00.920 --> 00:41:05.580
I always fall in love with the writers my whole life, going back to college, going back
我这一生总是爱上作家，从大学开始，甚至追溯到

1104
00:41:05.580 --> 00:41:06.180
to high school.
高中时期。

1105
00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:09.300
We fall in love with the things that we feel missing in ourselves.
我们爱上的往往是我们自身缺失的东西。

1106
00:41:09.680 --> 00:41:11.280
I think you're right, Ange.
我想你是对的，安吉。

1107
00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:14.080
Things are falling apart for Andy and Jim.
安迪和吉姆的情况正在恶化。

1108
00:41:14.260 --> 00:41:16.060
It's becoming very clear.
这一点变得非常明显。

1109
00:41:16.360 --> 00:41:18.440
How is Andy going to keep this going?
安迪打算怎么维持下去呢？

1110
00:41:19.060 --> 00:41:21.180
We got a fan question from Greg S.
我们收到了一位来自马里兰州的格雷格·S发来的粉丝提问，

1111
00:41:21.280 --> 00:41:22.140
in Maryland who said,
他说，

1112
00:41:22.160 --> 00:41:25.220
this episode has one of the best work-related quotes ever.
这一集里有史上最棒的职场语录之一。

1113
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:27.160
I am a video editor.
我是一名视频剪辑师。

1114
00:41:27.260 --> 00:41:31.080
And I cannot tell you how many times I'm asked to edit something, review the footage I'm
我无法告诉你我被要求剪辑某样东西，查看给我的素材时，

1115
00:41:31.080 --> 00:41:35.340
given, and I say to myself under my breath, I am not Rumpelstiltskin, Jim.
我私下里对自己说了多少次：吉姆，我可不是侏儒怪。

1116
00:41:35.460 --> 00:41:37.520
I can't keep spinning gold out of your shit.
我没法把你的垃圾变成金子。

1117
00:41:38.660 --> 00:41:39.960
It's such a good line.
这台词太棒了。

1118
00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:42.680
They are such a horrible lying duo.
他们俩真是对糟糕的撒谎精组合。

1119
00:41:43.020 --> 00:41:44.660
The two of them are so bad.
他们俩真是太差劲了。

1120
00:41:44.660 --> 00:41:50.340
Now it's escalated to this story where Andy, who lives by the courthouse, would drive every
现在事情升级到了这个地步：住在法院旁边的安迪，每天早上开车

1121
00:41:50.340 --> 00:41:54.780
morning and get Jim and bring him back to the courthouse and watch his cute tushy walk into
去接吉姆，把他带回法院，然后看着他那可爱的屁股走上

1122
00:41:54.780 --> 00:41:55.340
those steps.
那些台阶。

1123
00:41:56.100 --> 00:41:58.160
It's become like a nightmare for them.
这对他们来说简直成了噩梦。

1124
00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:02.620
There was a Dwight talking head here that didn't make it into the episode, but I want to read
这里原本有一个德怀特的采访片段没能放进正片里，但我很想读给

1125
00:42:02.620 --> 00:42:03.040
it to you.
你们听。

1126
00:42:03.140 --> 00:42:03.420
Okay.
好的。

1127
00:42:06.140 --> 00:42:07.160
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1128
00:42:07.340 --> 00:42:08.040
Dwight says,
德怀特说，

1129
00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:13.380
I have a recurring nightmare that I've been wrongly accused of a crime, and 12 of these
我经常做一个噩梦，梦见我被错误地指控犯罪，而陪审团里坐着12个

1130
00:42:13.380 --> 00:42:14.440
idiots are on the jury.
这样的白痴。

1131
00:42:14.780 --> 00:42:16.260
Stanley is fast asleep.
斯坦利在呼呼大睡。

1132
00:42:16.540 --> 00:42:18.120
Kevin eats the evidence.
凯文把证据给吃了。

1133
00:42:18.560 --> 00:42:21.520
Phyllis' name is Allison, but it really is Phyllis.
菲利斯的真名其实是艾莉森，但她确实就是菲利斯。

1134
00:42:21.960 --> 00:42:24.580
Jim is foreman of the jury and pronounces me guilty.
吉姆是陪审团团长，宣判我有罪。

1135
00:42:25.020 --> 00:42:28.300
The cop takes me away and tells me that I've been a bad boy.
警察把我带走，告诉我我一直是个坏孩子。

1136
00:42:28.760 --> 00:42:30.080
And we have sex in the hall.
然后我们在大厅里发生了关系。

1137
00:42:30.380 --> 00:42:32.260
She leaves the handcuffs on.
她没把手铐解开。

1138
00:42:32.460 --> 00:42:33.960
They take me away to prison.
他们把我带去监狱。

1139
00:42:34.180 --> 00:42:36.180
The guards are all women.
狱警全都是女性。

1140
00:42:36.680 --> 00:42:37.600
And then he goes,
然后他说，

1141
00:42:39.600 --> 00:42:41.980
That went places I wasn't expecting.
这走向真是出乎我的意料。

1142
00:42:42.160 --> 00:42:42.540
I know.
我知道。

1143
00:42:43.080 --> 00:42:47.720
And I had to wonder, too, if somewhere embedded in there was a little shout out to the fact
我也在想，这其中是否隐含着对艾莉森和菲利斯曾经共事过这一事实的

1144
00:42:47.720 --> 00:42:49.520
that Allison and Phyllis worked together.
一点小致敬。

1145
00:42:50.660 --> 00:42:51.700
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

1146
00:42:51.740 --> 00:42:52.620
Allison Jones.
艾莉森·琼斯。

1147
00:42:52.860 --> 00:42:53.080
Yep.
没错。

1148
00:42:53.320 --> 00:42:53.600
Hmm.
嗯。

1149
00:42:54.340 --> 00:42:56.220
Well, should we go back to the hospital?
那么，我们要回到医院了吗？

1150
00:42:56.740 --> 00:43:00.280
Yeah, because Erin is holding baby Philip, and she says,
好的，因为艾琳正抱着小菲利普，她说，

1151
00:43:00.420 --> 00:43:04.260
You know, I think Philip might be more than five pounds because that's the weight that
你知道吗，我觉得菲利普可能不止五磅，因为那是

1152
00:43:04.260 --> 00:43:05.180
I squat with.
我深蹲的重量。

1153
00:43:05.540 --> 00:43:08.280
And the senator just says, Oh, he's nine pounds.
然后参议员就说，哦，他有九磅重。

1154
00:43:08.700 --> 00:43:09.000
Yes.
是的。

1155
00:43:09.160 --> 00:43:11.080
And Angela's like, Oh, I don't know.
安吉拉就说，哦，我不知道。

1156
00:43:11.420 --> 00:43:12.400
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

1157
00:43:12.780 --> 00:43:15.820
Well, Angela makes up an excuse for remembering it wrong.
好吧，安吉拉为自己记错找了个借口。

1158
00:43:15.980 --> 00:43:17.300
You know, she was on so many drugs.
你知道，她当时用了太多药了。

1159
00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:20.060
Yeah, she might as well have been at a James Taylor concert.
是啊，她当时的状态简直就像在詹姆斯·泰勒的演唱会上一样。

1160
00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:25.340
Well, now Oscar and Kevin are going to give Angela some gifts that they brought for baby
好了，现在奥斯卡和凯文要给安吉拉送上他们为宝宝

1161
00:43:25.340 --> 00:43:25.680
Philip.
菲利普准备的礼物了。

1162
00:43:26.240 --> 00:43:29.320
We got a fan question from Kelly T in Indiana who says,
我们收到一个来自印第安纳州凯莉·T的粉丝提问，她说：

1163
00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:33.580
When Oscar gives Angela the present at the hospital, it is in the classic movie present
当奥斯卡在医院给安吉拉送礼物时，那是一个经典的电影式礼物

1164
00:43:33.580 --> 00:43:34.080
box.
盒。

1165
